    {
      "v": 7,
      "zh": "耶和华对约伯说话以后，就对提幔人以利法说：「我的怒气向你和你两个朋友发作，因为你们议论我不如我的仆人约伯说的是。",
      "en": "After the Lord had spoken these things to Job, he[NOTE:1] said to Eliphaz the Temanite, “My anger is stirred up[NOTE:2] against you and your two friends because you have not spoken about me what is right,[NOTE:3] as my servant Job has.",
      "notes": [
        "Heb “the Lord.” The title has been replaced by the pronoun (“he”) in the translation for stylistic reasons.",
        "Heb “is kindled.”",
        "The form נְכוֹנָה (nekhonah) is from כּוּן (kun, “to be firm; to be fixed; to be established”). Here it means “the right thing” or “truth.” The Akkadian cognate kīnu means “true, just, honest, firm” (CAD K: 389)."
